Great — minimal, low-risk, visible change. I’ll give you one tiny standalone custom pipe (genreList) and the two smallest edits you need to make to show a custom pipe is implemented:

add the pipe file

import the pipe into MovieCardComponent imports

replace the existing genre text in the movie-card template with the pipe


That’s it — no other files or modules to touch.


---

1) Create the pipe file

Path: src/app/shared/pipes/genre.pipe.ts
Contents: (copy-paste exactly)

import { Pipe, PipeTransform } from '@angular/core';

@Pipe({
  name: 'genreList',
  standalone: true
})
export class GenrePipe implements PipeTransform {
  transform(genres: string[] | null | undefined): string {
    if (!Array.isArray(genres) || genres.length === 0) return '';
    return genres.join(', ');
  }
}

This is a tiny, safe pipe that converts ["Action","Drama"] → "Action, Drama".


---

2) Add the pipe to the MovieCard component imports

Open:
src/app/features/movies/movie-card/movie-card.component.ts

Add an import at the top (adjust relative path if your folders differ):

import { GenrePipe } from '../../../shared/pipes/genre.pipe';

Then include the pipe in the imports array of the @Component metadata. Example snippet:

@Component({
  selector: 'app-movie-card',
  standalone: true,
  imports: [CommonModule, RouterModule, /* other imports */, GenrePipe],
  templateUrl: './movie-card.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./movie-card.component.scss']
})
export class MovieCardComponent { ... }

(If your file already imports other pipes/directives, just add GenrePipe to that list.)


---

3) Use the pipe in the movie-card template

Open: src/app/features/movies/movie-card/movie-card.component.html

Find where genres are shown (something like {{ movie?.genre?.join(', ') }} or similar). Replace that fragment with:

<div class="genres" *ngIf="movie?.genre?.length">
  {{ movie?.genre | genreList }}
</div>

If there was no explicit genre display before, add the whole block in the info area so it’s visibly present under the title.


---

4) Test it

Run (or reload) your dev server:

ng serve

Open the home or movie-list page and confirm each card now shows the genre text formatted by the pipe (e.g., Action, Adventure).


